><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Liang</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Grishin</surname><given-names>NV</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldstein</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Identification of the acyltransferase that octanoylates ghrelin, an appetite stimulating peptide hormone.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>132</volume><fpage>387</fpage><lpage>396</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18267071</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-DeVriese1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Vriese</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gregoire</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>De Neef</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Robberecht</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Delporte</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Ghrelin is produced by the human erythroleukemic HEL cell line and involved in an autocrine pathway leading to cell proliferation.</article-title><source>Endocrinology</source><volume>146</volume><fpage>1514</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15564328</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Hosoda1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hosoda</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kojima</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsuo</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kangawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Ghrelin and des-acyl ghrelin: two major forms of rat ghrelin peptide in gastrointestinal tissue.</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><volume>279</volume><fpage>909</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11162448</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Eberwine1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eberwine</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Barchas</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hewlett</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Isolation of enzyme cDNA clones by enzyme immunodetection assay: isolation of a peptide acetyltransferase.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>84</volume><fpage>1449</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3469677</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Woodford1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Woodford</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Dixon</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1979</year><article-title>The Nalpha-acetylation of corticotropin and fragments of corticotropin by a rat pituitary Nalpha-acetyltransferase.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>254</volume><fpage>4993</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">221456</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Glembotski1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glembotski</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1982</year><article-title>Characterization of the peptide acetyltransferase activity in bovine and rat intermediate pituitaries responsible for the acetylation of beta-endorphin and alpha-melanotropin.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>257</volume><fpage>10501</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6286657</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Boutin1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boutin</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Myristoylation.</article-title><source>Cell Signal</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9067626</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Liu1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Dudler</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gelb</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Purification of a protein palmitoyltransferase that acts on H-Ras protein and on a C-terminal N-Ras peptide.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>271</volume><fpage>23269</fpage><lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8798525</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Chen1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Hyatt</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mucenski</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Mason</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Shannon</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Identification and characterization of a lysophosphatidylcholine acyltransferase in alveolar type II cells.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>103</volume><fpage>11724</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16864775</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Zhao1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhao</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>YQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonacci</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bredt</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Identification and characterization of a major liver lysophosphatidylcholine acyltransferase.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>283</volume><fpage>8258</fpage><lpage>65</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18195019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Hofmann1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hofmann</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>A superfamily of membrane-bound O-acyltransferases with implications for wnt signaling.</article-title><source>Trends Biochem Sci</source><volume>25</volume><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10694878</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Takada1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Takada</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Satomi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kurata</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ueno</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Norioka</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Monounsaturated fatty acid modification of Wnt protein: its role in Wnt secretion.</article-title><source>Dev Cell</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>791</fpage><lpage>801</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17141155</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Yang2"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhao</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldstein</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Inhibition of ghrelin O-acyltransferase (GOAT) by octanoylated pentapeptides.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>105</volume><fpage>10750</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18669668</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Lindberg1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lindberg</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Shaw</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Finley</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Leone</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Deininger</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Posttranslational modifications of rat proenkephalin overexpressed in Chinese hamster ovary cells.</article-title><source>Endocrinology</source><volume>128</volume><fpage>1849</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2004604</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Ozawa1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ozawa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cai</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindberg</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Production of bioactive peptides in an in vitro system.</article-title><source>Anal Biochem</source><volume>366</volume><fpage>182</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17540328</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005426-Higgens1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Higgens</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1966</year><article-title>The uptake of lipids by rat liver cells.</article-title><source>Biochem J.</source><volume>99</volume><fpage>631</fpage><lpage>639</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5964960</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>This work was supported in part by DA05084 to I. Lindberg. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>